w('refusal.VERSION_RELATIONSHIP_DISAGREES', 'That version says its evidence fits together one way and is grouped the other way. The two cannot both be true, and a member accepting it would be signing for a reading that is not the one written down.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_PARTITION_INCOMPLETE', "Some of that version's evidence has not been placed in the argument. A part nobody placed sitting beside parts somebody did is a relationship the record would have to guess at, and it would have to guess in the direction that makes the finding stronger.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_GROUND_UNASSERTED', "That version claims one part of its argument would carry the answer on its own, and no member has said so. That claim is the one thing that makes a finding stronger, so it carries the name of the person making it and the date they made it — never a machine's.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_DERIVED_FROM_UNKNOWN', 'That version says it came from a version this inquiry does not have. Where a version came from is how the alternatives are read as a tree rather than a pile, so it names one that exists or it names none.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_DERIVATION_CYCLE', 'These versions say they were derived from each other in a loop, so there is no answer to which came first. Versions form a tree, and a tree has a root.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_REGROUP_UNATTRIBUTED', 'That version rearranges the argument it was derived from, and nobody has said who did it or why. Rearranging which evidence is grouped with which changes how strong the finding reads, so it is an act with a name on it rather than an edit.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_LEG_NOT_CITABLE', 'One part of that version rests on something that cannot be evidence for a question — the record admits a document or another question, and nothing else.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_FROZEN', 'That version already exists and has been changed in place. A version is frozen once written, because two people comparing it must be comparing the same thing — so an edit becomes a NEW version derived from this one, and the original stays exactly as it was.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_STATE_UNKNOWN', 'That version is in a state the record has no name for. A version is suggested, being considered, accepted, or rejected — and nothing else.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_HIDDEN_NOT_BOOLEAN', 'The setting that hides a version from the display is not a yes-or-no answer here. Hiding a version removes it from view and nothing else — it stays in the record and stays answerable — so there is no third thing for this to say.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_LEG_SELF', 'That version rests on the question it is an answer to. A question is not evidence for its own answer.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_ORPHAN_ROW', 'Part of the version block names a version that is not there. It would be material the record holds and never shows anybody, which is worse than not holding it.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_LEG_UNRESOLVED', 'One part of that version rests on something this record does not hold. A reading of the evidence that points at a document nobody can open is a reading nobody can check.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.BASIS_VERSIONS_NO_INQUIRY', 'That request did not say which question to read the versions of. A version is one reading of the evidence for one question, so it asks rather than answering for a question you did not name.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.BASIS_VERSIONS_NOT_AN_INQUIRY', 'Only a question carries versions of its evidence, and that is not a question. Answering with an empty list would say this thing has no readings of its evidence, when the truth is that it could not have any.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_DISPOSITION_UNATTRIBUTED', "This reading of the evidence was set aside or turned down with no reason recorded, or with a machine's name against it. What a member decided about a reading, and why, is the record itself — a decision nobody signed and nobody explained leaves nothing to answer to.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_ACT_NO_INQUIRY', 'That request did not say which question the reading belongs to. A reading of the evidence always belongs to one question, so it asks rather than guessing.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_ACT_NOT_AN_INQUIRY', 'Only a question carries readings of its evidence, and that is not a question. There is nothing here to accept, set aside or turn down.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_ACT_NO_VERSION', 'That request did not name which reading to act on. A question can hold several readings of its evidence, and acting on the wrong one is worse than being asked which you meant.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_ACT_NO_SUCH_VERSION', 'This question holds no reading by that name. Readings are named so a member can ask for one by name, and a name nobody wrote is refused rather than matched to whatever is nearest.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_MOVE_VERSION', "Deciding what to do with a reading of the evidence is a named member's call, and this request came from an automated credential. A machine may put a reading forward and may never settle it. Sign in as a member.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_ILLEGAL_TRANSITION', 'That is not a move this reading can make from where it stands. A reading a member has already accepted is corrected by turning it down or by putting it back under consideration, never by returning it to something nobody had acted on.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_NO_REASON', "Setting a reading aside or turning it down carries the reason in the member's own words. The record of what was turned down is the instrument that makes a pattern of turning things down visible at all, and it is worth nothing without the reason.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_REASON_MALFORMED', 'That reason was given but could not be stored as written: it is either longer than the record allows or it contains a character the record has no way to escape, such as a double quote. Nothing was changed. Shorten it, or say it without the quotation marks, and the words stay yours.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_BASIS_CYCLE', 'Accepting this reading would make the question rest, through a chain of other questions, on itself. The answer would then be its own support, which is a circle rather than a case, and the chain that closes it is named above.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_NOT_ACCEPTED', "A project can only stand on a reading its members have accepted, and this one has not been accepted. Exploring an unsettled reading is done by calculating over it, which moves nobody's stance.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_CURRENT_NO_PROJECT', "Standing on a reading is something a PROJECT does, so this request has to name which project. A question can be shared by several projects, and one project's decision must never quietly move another project's.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_CURRENT_UNRELATED', 'That project does not draw on this question, so it has no stance here to move. Add the question to the project first, and then choose what the project stands on.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.VERSION_ACT_UNWRITABLE', "This question's own file could not be rewritten in place, so nothing was changed. Acting on a reading edits the record the reading lives in, and a half-written record is worse than an unchanged one.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PUBLISHED_CANNOT_MOVE_VERSION', 'This question has been published, and the case it went out in froze it as it stood. Changing which reading of the evidence it stands on now would leave the published version saying something the question no longer says. Pick it back up first, make the change, and publish that as a new edition — the published one keeps its own signature and goes on answering.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('basis-versions.basis_version', "a new version of the inquiry's basis — the main output: a complete alternative composition with its legs, its branches and its description (section 6)", note='basis-versions, basis-version')
w('basis-versions.sharpen_question', "the inquiry asks two questions that need different evidence; here they are separated (section 8). The separation is carried as the version's claim", note='basis-versions, sharpen-question')
w('basis-versions.new_inquiry', "a proposition answering the question, with the first version of its basis (section 8, under section 3's basis ruling)", note='basis-versions, new-inquiry')
w('basis-versions.level_empty', "we looked at this level — meaning, content, documents, or the open internet — and it is empty, with the observation-log address of the search that establishes it. Without this kind a run that honestly found nothing supportable is indistinguishable from a run that emitted nothing (SWEEP section 6), and section 15's empty-run instrument has no object to count", note='basis-versions, level-empty')
w('basis-versions.new_edition', "evidence bearing on a PUBLISHED finding. A published case cannot be changed, so the only act available is a new edition, and it is the member's", note='basis-versions, new-edition')
w('refusal.VERSION_KIND_UNKNOWN', 'This reading says it is a kind of suggestion nobody recognizes. The kinds are a closed set because what a suggestion CLAIMS to be decides how it is read, and a kind outside the set is a claim with nothing behind it.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_CONCLUDE', 'A conclusion is a person saying what they think the record shows, and it carries their name for as long as the record lasts. The credential that asked here is an automated one: it may raise the question, gather what bears on it and draft the answer, and it may never be the one who answers. Sign in to conclude.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NO_CONCLUSION', 'Concluding records what was concluded, and this one says nothing. If the honest answer is that the team could not settle it, write that down — an answer of undetermined is a real answer here and is stated rather than left blank.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NO_FALSIFIER', 'A conclusion has to say what would overturn it. Without that nobody can check the finding, including the person who wrote it, and a finding that cannot be checked claims more than the evidence behind it can carry. If no falsifier can honestly be named, say so rather than inventing one: the record will carry that no falsifier was stated, in your name and with the date, wherever this finding appears.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.FALSIFIER_AND_NONE_STATED', 'You have written a falsifier and also asked to record that none could be stated. Those are two different things to say about this finding, and choosing between them is not something the record should do on your behalf. Keep the falsifier, or clear it and record the absence.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.CONCLUSION_IS_THE_CLAIM', 'When a project concludes, the claim it adopts is the conclusion, so a separate conclusion text is not accepted — it could say something no claim said. Anything you want to add beyond the claim can be sent as commentary: it is recorded in your name and is never treated as evidence.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.BAD_BIAS_APPLIED', "A project's conclusion can record each statement of its declared bias that bore on it: the statement, and whether it refused an inference or raised scrutiny. This list could not be recorded as sent (a missing or unwritable statement, another effect, a repeat, or more than 32), or it was sent with no project. Nothing was recorded.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NOTHING_TO_WITHDRAW', 'There is no conclusion here to withdraw: this project has not concluded this question, or has already withdrawn its latest conclusion. Everything it concluded and withdrew before stays in the record.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.UNSPLICEABLE_CONCLUSIONS', "The project's own record is laid out in a way this act cannot add a conclusion to without rewriting parts of it nobody asked to change, so nothing was recorded. The project's file needs its list of conclusions tidied before it can conclude.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_NO_INQUIRY', "That request does not name a question this record holds and you can read. Making a citation more specific happens on a question's reading of its evidence, so it needs the question first.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_NO_SUCH_VERSION', 'That question has no reading of its evidence by that name. A citation is made more specific in a NEW reading taken from an existing one, so the reading it starts from has to be named exactly as the question holds it.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_NO_SUCH_LEG', 'That reading has no piece of evidence at the position named. Pieces are counted from zero, in the order the reading lists them.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_NO_PART', 'That piece of evidence has no part to point at more precisely. It either rests on another question, which has no pages or passages, or on a document this record holds no copy of — and a part of something nobody captured cannot be named.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_NOT_A_MEMBER', "Making a citation more specific is a member's own act, done in their name. A machine may PROPOSE passages that look relevant, and they are listed for you to choose from, but choosing which passage is on point is a judgment a person signs for.", note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_NO_EXTENT', 'That request does not say which part of the document the citation should point at. Name the part — a page, a region of a page, a cell, a paragraph or a slide — or choose one of the proposed passages by its content id.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_BAD_EXTENT', 'The part named cannot be recorded as sent: it names a field this act does not take, a value that cannot be written into the record, a content id this record does not hold, or both a content id and a description of the same part. It is refused rather than guessed at, because a citation quietly re-read would not be the one you made.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_OTHER_CAPTURE', 'The part named is not in the copy of the document this citation rests on. Pointing the citation at a different document, or at a later copy of the same one, is not making it more specific — it is moving it, and a citation is never moved except by its own separate act.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_NOT_NARROWER', 'The part named is not inside what the citation already points at — it is the same part, a wider one, or a different place in the document. Making a citation more specific can only ever point it at LESS of the document than before; anything else would claim a precision nobody established.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_NAME', 'The new reading needs a name of its own, one the question does not already use. The reading it starts from keeps its name and stays exactly as it was: changing an existing reading in place would move a citation somebody else may be relying on.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NARROW_NO_DESCRIPTION', 'The new reading needs a short account of what changed and why — which citation now points at less of its document, and what makes that part the one that matters. That account is what a later reader has to go on.', note='basis-versions, refusal by its code')
w('basis-versions.text.added', 'a {field} was added', note='basis-versions, text')
w('basis-versions.text.removed', 'a {field} was removed', note='basis-versions, text')
w('basis-versions.undetermined_claim.conclusion_names_reading', "this conclusion names reading '{nv}' and a claim, but {recorded}, so which claim was concluded cannot be established from the record and is undetermined — never taken on the frontmatter's word.", note='basis-versions, BasisVersions.undeterminedClaim()#0')
w('basis-versions.undetermined_claim.inquiry_carries_reading', 'the inquiry carries no such reading', note='basis-versions, BasisVersions.undeterminedClaim()#0')
w('basis-versions.undetermined_claim.reading_state_claim', 'that reading does not state the claim recorded', note='basis-versions, BasisVersions.undeterminedClaim()#0')
w('basis-versions.text.stands_reading', '{pid} stands on reading', note='basis-versions, text')
w('basis-versions.text.conclusion_names_reading', 'this conclusion names reading', note='basis-versions, text')
w('basis-versions.says.record_reading_document', "the record's own reading of this document found a reference ('{ref}') at {ref2}. That it is there is what the reading says; whether it is on point is yours to judge.", note='basis-versions, says')
w('basis-versions.says.machine_proposed_passage', 'a machine proposed this passage in run {run}. It is a PROPOSAL: not part of any citation, and not coverage, until a member chooses it.', note='basis-versions, says')
w('basis-versions.says.machine_marked_passage', 'a machine marked this passage citable. Nobody has chosen it for this citation.', note='basis-versions, says')
w('basis-versions.says.copy_document_read', 'this copy of the document has never been read, so the machine has no passage to propose. You may still name the part yourself.', note='basis-versions, says')
w('basis-versions.says.document_read_machine', 'the document was read and nothing the machine found lies inside what this citation already points at. That is not evidence there is no better passage — only that none was proposed. You may still name the part yourself.', note='basis-versions, says')
w('basis-versions.says.entry_machine_work', "every entry here is MACHINE WORK and a PROPOSAL. Listing it wrote nothing and cited nothing; which passage is on point to this question is the member's judgment, made by op=narrow in the member's own name.", note='basis-versions, says')
w('basis-versions.says.new_reading_written', "a new reading '{name_written}' was written, taken from '{vname}', with piece {k} pointing at less of its document. '{vname}' and its citation are exactly as they were. The new reading is SUGGESTED: standing on it is a separate act.", note='basis-versions, says')
w('refusal.NO_SUCH_EVENT', 'No event with that id is held in the record, so nothing can be said about it or attached to it. Name an event the record holds. Nothing was written.', note='events, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NO_SUCH_DATED_FACT', 'No date a document states is held under that id where you can see it, so nothing can rest on it. Name a dated fact the record holds. Nothing was written.', note='events, refusal by its code')
w('events.rows.source_value_changed', "the source's own value changed", note='events, k.rows()#4')
w('events.why.list_holds_event', 'a {endpoint} list holds no event, item or vote to write', note='events, why')
w('events.why.bodyid_resolves_registered', 'its BodyId resolves to no registered body', note='events, why')
w('events.why.active_profile_gives', "no active profile gives a time zone, so the meeting's time is not placed", note='events, =why')
w('events.rows.source_date_time', "the source's own date or time changed", note='events, k.rows()#3')
w('events.rows.earlier_publication_value', 'an earlier publication value was observed', note='events, k.rows()#3')
w('events.why.meeting_held_import', 'its meeting is not held: import the meeting first', note='events, why')
w('events.why.source_names_personid', 'the source names no PersonId that resolves to a registered entity', note='events, why')
w('events.why.item_held_import', 'its item is not held: import the items first', note='events, why')
w('events.why.personid_resolves_registered', 'its PersonId resolves to no registered entity', note='events, why')
w('events.why.register_assigns_entry', 'the register assigns this entry no id', note='events, why')
w('events.when_why', "the entry's date was not read as a day", note='events, when_why')
w('events.label.text', 'on or before', note='events, label')
w('events.why.capture_class_opt', 'this capture class is not in the opt-in set', note='events, why')
w('events.why.record_holds_capture', 'the record holds no such capture', note='events, why')
w('events.transact.file_writes', '; {by} as the file writes it: {who}', note='events, record.transact()#0')
w('events.transact.last_modified', 'last modified by', note='events, record.transact()#0')
w('events.text.member_testimony', "a member's testimony", note='events, text')
w('events.says.states_caused', '{source} states that one caused the other', note='events, says')
w('events.vote_value_why', 'no active jurisdiction profile names vote values, so the value is kept as the record writes it', note='events, vote_value_why')
w('events.why.dated_attestation_see', 'no dated attestation you can see governs this event', note='events, =why')
w('events.why.placed_nowhere_attestation', 'placed nowhere: no attestation of this event is dated', note='events, =why')
w('events.why.cited_orders_disagree', 'the cited orders disagree', note='events, why')
w('events.says.cited_relation_states', 'the cited relation states which came first; the dates held do not settle it', note='events, says')
w('events.und.proceeding_kind_held', "the proceeding's kind is not held, so no flow can be read for it", note='events, und()#0')
w('events.und.active_profile_holds', 'no active profile holds a flow for proceedings of kind {kind}', note='events, und()#0')
w('events.und.held_event_bears', "no held event bears on this proceeding's flow on that date", note='events, und()#0')
w('events.und.order_deciding_events', 'the order of the deciding events against that date is undetermined at the precision held', note='events, und()#0')
w('events.present', 'was present at', note='events, present')
w('events.copied', 'was copied on', note='events, copied')
w('events.party', 'was a party to', note='events, party')
w('events.subject.subject', 'was the subject of', note='events, subject')
w('events.stated_cause', 'is stated by a source to cause', note='events, stated_cause')
w('events.within', 'took place within', note='events, within')
w('events.precedes', 'is cited as coming before', note='events, precedes')
w('events.why.placed_nowhere_event', 'placed nowhere: an event with no dated attestation has no when', note='events, why')
w('events.text.held_zone_span', 'a when held with no zone has no span, so which came first is not settled', note='events, text')
w('events.text.upper_bound_says', 'an upper bound says only "on or before", so which came first is not settled', note='events, text')
w('events.why.precision_held_settle', 'the precision held does not settle the order', note='events, why')
w('events.population', 'these are the held uses you may see, never every use made: a population, not a census', note='events, =POPULATION')
w('events.text.document_see', 'in a document you cannot see', note='events, text')
w('events.text.cited_passage_words', 'in the cited passage, its words not read', note='events, text')
w('events.text.date_recorded', 'date not recorded', note='events, text')
w('events.text.provision_recorded', 'provision not recorded', note='events, text')
w('events.says.assessment_against', 'Assessment of {subject} by {by}, {date}, against {standard}: {result}', note='events, says')
w('events.says.subject_recorded', 'subject not recorded', note='events, says')
w('events.says.standard_found_unmet', 'no standard found unmet', note='events, says')
w('events.text.reason_stated', 'no reason stated', note='events, text')
w('events.says.discretion_used', 'Discretion used by {by}, {date}, {why}', note='events, =says')
w('events.says.waiver_waived', 'Waiver {outcome} by {by}, {date}, {why}; waived: {scope}; {conditions}; {expiry}', note='events, =says')
w('events.text.conditions_stated', 'no conditions stated', note='events, text')
w('events.text.expiry_stated', 'no expiry stated', note='events, text')
w('refusal.CAPTURE_NOT_DRAINING', "Only the background worker of your team's Civicsmith fetches documents, and it does so from its own queue. Nothing else can ask it to fetch something right now — including the assistant that asked for the document in the first place.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.RENDER_FLAG_MALFORMED', "This request asked for a rendered capture in a form your team's Civicsmith does not recognize. It answers render: true or nothing, so a request for the page as a visitor saw it is never quietly answered with the page's empty frame. Nothing was fetched.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.RENDER_ARM_CONFLICT', 'A rendered capture runs the live page in a browser, and this request combined that with a way of capturing that does not load a live page (an archived copy, a Drive export, or the continuation of an earlier capture). Ask for one or the other. Nothing was fetched.', note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.RENDER_NO_RENDERER', "Your team's Civicsmith has no working page renderer, so it cannot capture the page as a visitor saw it. Nothing was fetched, and the page's empty frame was not filed in its place.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.RENDER_DEFERRED', "Today's allowance for rendering pages is fully committed — either already used, or held by renders your team's Civicsmith is running right now — so this render is deferred, and that is recorded. Nothing was fetched and nothing was filed in its place. Try again when the renders in flight have finished, or after midnight UTC.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.RENDER_HOST_COOLING_OFF', "Your team's Civicsmith is giving that website a rest after it asked us to slow down, and a rendered capture loads the page again, so it was not attempted. Nothing was fetched. Try again after the wait shown beside this message.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.RENDER_NOT_A_PAGE', 'The address served something that is not a web page a browser can render, such as a PDF or an office file, so there is nothing for a rendered capture to add. Nothing was filed. Capture it the ordinary way.', note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.RENDER_FAILED', "The page was fetched but the renderer did not produce the page as a visitor would see it, so nothing was filed: the page's empty frame is never filed as its content. The reason the renderer gave is beside this message.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.RENDER_AT_CAPACITY', "Your team's Civicsmith is already rendering as many pages at once as it allows, so this render is waiting for one of them to finish. Nothing was fetched and nothing was filed in its place. A scheduled capture asks again on its own; try again in a minute.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.DRIVE_HOP_FACT_SUPPLIED', "This request tried to tell the record where a document was exported from, in what format, or by whom. Those are facts your team's Civicsmith establishes by doing the fetch itself, never facts it accepts from whoever asked. Send the Drive link and nothing else.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.DRIVE_FOLDER_NOT_A_DOCUMENT', 'That address is a Drive FOLDER — a listing of files rather than a document. There is nothing to export and no single set of bytes a capture of it would hold. Name the document you want; harvesting everything a folder lists is a different act.', note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.DRIVE_KIND_UNDETERMINED', 'That Drive address names a file but not what KIND of file it is, and the kind is what decides which export to ask for. Guessing would file bytes in a format nobody established. Use the address that opens the document itself, which carries the kind.', note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.DRIVE_SHAPE_UNRECOGNISED', "That is a Google Drive address in a form your team's Civicsmith does not recognize. Rather than capture whatever bytes the address happens to serve and call it the document, it says so. If this shape should be harvestable, that is a change worth making deliberately.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.DRIVE_EXPORT_IS_THE_SHELL', 'Google answered the export address with a web page rather than a document — which is what it does when a file is not shared with anyone who has the link. That page is the application, not the document, and it is not filed as one. Check that the file is shared.', note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.DRIVE_EXPORT_UNREACHABLE', 'The OpenDocument export of that Drive document could not be fetched, so nothing was captured. The application page at the same address is NOT captured instead: a record holding the app in place of the document would look like evidence and be none.', note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.DRIVE_EXPORT_BYTES_ARE_THE_SHELL', "The export address said it was sending a document and sent a web page instead. Your team's Civicsmith checks the bytes rather than taking the label, so the application page was recognized and refused. Nothing was filed under that document address.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.EVIDENCE_STORAGE_NOT_CONFIGURED', "Your team's Civicsmith was installed without the storage it keeps captured documents in, so it cannot keep or read the bytes of a captured document. That is a fact about how your team's Civicsmith was set up, not about this request: whoever installed it can connect that storage in the hosting account. Nothing was changed.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.SWEEP_SCOPE_MISSING', "A sweep asked your team's Civicsmith to fetch a document without saying which sites the sweep may reach, so nothing was fetched. A sweep only ever fetches within the scope members ratified for it.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.SWEEP_REDIRECT_OUT_OF_SCOPE', "The page this sweep fetched sent it on to an address outside the sweep's ratified scope. The sweep did not follow it: nothing there was fetched and nothing was filed. Members can widen the scope if that address belongs in it.", note='acquisition, refusal by its code')
