w('refusal.ATTRIBUTION_NOT_A_MEMBER', "How a member's observation is attributed is that member's own choice. The credential that asked is an automated one, and it cannot make that choice for anybody. Sign in and choose it yourself.", note='case-tensions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.ATTRIBUTION_NO_LEVEL', 'No level was chosen. Choose what a published case shows of who said your observation: the team, the project, the cover the team knows you by, or your handle. Nothing is filled in for you.', note='case-tensions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.ATTRIBUTION_LEVEL_UNKNOWN', 'That is not one of the four levels. Choose team, project, cover or name.', note='case-tensions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.ATTRIBUTION_NOT_AN_OBSERVATION', "That is not a member's firsthand observation in this record, nor material from a source this case shows as Withheld, so there is no author or attesting member whose choice this is. Attribution is chosen for those only.", note='case-tensions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.ATTRIBUTION_NOT_THE_AUTHOR', 'Another member recorded that observation, or attested that material. Only the member who said it, or who attested it, chooses how a published case credits them — not a project owner, not an administrator, and not a default.', note='case-tensions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.ATTRIBUTION_AUTHOR_NOT_ACTIVE', "That observation's author is not an active member, and nobody chooses for them. The observation stays in the record and can be used where its author already chose, and nowhere new.", note='case-tensions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.ATTRIBUTION_NOT_REACHED', 'No prepared case edition by that name rests on your observation. You choose an attribution for an edition that uses your words, once its case document has been prepared.', note='case-tensions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.ATTRIBUTION_EDITION_RATIFIED', 'That edition is already signed, and a signed edition does not change. Your choice can apply to the next edition, which keeps your last choice until you change it.', note='case-tensions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.ATTRIBUTION_NAME_NO_HANDLE', 'Choosing your name publishes the handle you appear under in this record, and you have none. Choose another level, or set a handle first.', note='case-tensions, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.ATTRIBUTION_NO_REASON', 'Choosing how a published case shows who said your observation records why, in your own words, and no reason was given, or it is longer than 2,000 characters. Write one. Nothing was written.', note='case-tensions, refusal by its code')
w('case-tensions.says.contradiction_found_published', "each is a contradiction found on what a published case's findings rest on, one level deep, that its latest edition did not disclose, or one it disclosed that has since been resolved. The signed edition does not change; a later edition discloses or resolves it. No strength is composed.", note='case-tensions, says')
w('case-tensions.why.version_pinned', 'no version was pinned', note='case-tensions, why')
w('case-tensions.why.author_chosen_level', 'its author has chosen no level for this edition or any earlier one', note='case-tensions, why')
w('case-tensions.why.author_chose_edition', "its author chose '{level}' at edition {edition}, and the record holds no {level3} for them to publish under it", note='case-tensions, why')
w('case-tensions.why.case_document_carries', 'this case document carries no attribution statements to re-author', note='case-tensions, why')
w('case-tensions.why.case_document_re', 'the case document could not be re-authored here', note='case-tensions, why')
w('case-tensions.stated.edition_now_states', "edition {ed} of {cid} now states {subject} at level '{lv}'. The case document was re-authored; its owner signs the new bytes. A later edition inherits this choice until you change it.", note='case-tensions, stated')
w('case-tensions.why.unsigned_case_document', 'no unsigned case document is held for this edition', note='case-tensions, why')
w('case-tensions.why.case_document_states', 'this case document states no attestation row of yours for that capture', note='case-tensions, why')
w('refusal.LEAD_NOT_EVIDENCE', 'That leg points at a LEAD. A lead is somewhere to look — what a member was told or suspects — and it is never evidence, so nothing can rest on it. Follow the lead: if the look finds the document, capture it and cite THAT; if you saw the thing yourself, write it up as your own observation.', note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NOT_INQUIRIES', 'This act moves a question along, and the selection carries things that are not questions. The whole set is refused rather than quietly narrowed to the part that fits, because a set that acted on less than you selected is a set you were not shown.', note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.SELF_BASIS', 'A question cannot be the evidence for its own answer. This write would have it rest on itself, which reads as support and adds nothing anybody outside could check.', note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.BASIS_CYCLE', 'This write would close a loop: the chain it would join already rests, somewhere further along, on the thing being written. The path is named so the loop can be seen rather than re-derived, and support that circles back is support that rests on nothing.', note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_DIVIDE', "Dividing a question says the team asked one thing when it was really asking two, and that is a judgment about the team's own work. The credential that asked here is an automated one: it may raise questions and gather what they rest on, and may not restructure them. Sign in to divide it.", note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_GROUND', 'Grounding says some of the reasons behind an answer are strong enough to carry it on their own, and it is the one act here that makes a finding stronger rather than weaker. That decision needs a person behind it, and the credential that asked is an automated one. Sign in to ground it.', note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.IMPORTED_LEG_MALFORMED', "A leg on another team's finding names that finding and one edition, and nothing else: its grades are that edition's. Correct the leg. Nothing was written.", note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.STANDARD_LEG_AXIS', 'A leg on a standard rests on the text of that law as the team captured it, so the only grade it carries is the one that text earns. A connection, a testimony or a hunch is a different kind of claim. Correct the leg. Nothing was written.', note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.CALCULATION_LEG_MALFORMED', 'A leg on a calculation names the calculation and nothing else: how strong it is comes from the figures it was worked from, so the leg states no grade and names no part of its own. Correct the leg. Nothing was written.', note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.OCCURRENCE_LEG_MALFORMED', "A leg on a duty's occurrence names the duty and that one occurrence, and nothing else: how strong it is comes from the law that sets the duty and the dates that started and end it, so the leg states no grade, names no part, and is not listed among the references. Correct the leg. Nothing was written.", note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.DERIVED_LEG_MALFORMED', 'A leg on a connection the record worked out names that connection and the five facts it was worked out from: what kind it is, its two ends, the date it holds as of, and the method. Its name must be the one those five give, and it states no grade or part of its own: how strong it is comes from the links it was worked out over. Correct the leg. Nothing was written.', note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.BIAS_APPLICATION_MALFORMED', "A leg can record each statement of your project's declared bias that was applied to it: the statement, and what it did, which is one of three things: it lowered the leg's grade (from one letter to a weaker one), it set the leg aside, or it refused an inference. This record of it is not in that form. Recording it moves no grade: the grade on the leg is still the one you state. Correct the record. Nothing was written.", note='inquiry-grammar, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.TARGET_NOT_JOINED', 'An owner of a project is one of its participants who has joined it, and the member you named has not joined this project: they are invited and have not joined, have asked to leave, or hold no place in it. Nothing was changed. Once they have joined, they can be made an owner.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.LAST_OWNER', 'A project always has at least one owner, so the last one cannot be removed — the result would be work nobody is answerable for. Add another owner first, or stand the project down.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PROJECT_DIRECTORY_NEEDS_A_MEMBER', 'The list of projects you can ask to join is for a signed-in member. Sign in as yourself to see it.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PROJECT_REQUEST_NEEDS_A_MEMBER', 'Asking to join a project, withdrawing that request and reading your own requests are things a signed-in member does for themselves. Sign in as yourself to do it. Nothing was changed.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PROJECT_REQUEST_NOT_OUTSIDE', 'You can already see this project, so there is nothing to ask. If you were invited, join it with its checkbox. Nothing was changed.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PROJECT_REQUEST_ALREADY_OPEN', 'You already have a request open to join this project. Its owners answer it; you can withdraw it and ask again. Nothing was changed.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PROJECT_REQUEST_NONE_OPEN', 'There is no open request to join here to act on. It may already have been answered, withdrawn or lapsed. Nothing was changed.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PROJECT_REQUEST_ANSWER_NOT_THE_OWNER', 'Only an owner of this project can grant or decline a request to join it. Administrators see requests and answer none. Nothing was changed.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PROJECT_REQUEST_UNKNOWN_ANSWER', 'A request to join is either granted or declined, and nothing else. Choose one of the two. Nothing was changed.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PROJECT_REQUEST_REQUESTER_INACTIVE', 'The member who asked is no longer active, so they cannot be invited. The request stays open; you can decline it. Nothing was changed.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PROJECT_REQUEST_REQUESTER_ALREADY_A_PARTICIPANT', 'The member who asked is already a participant of this project, so granting would invite nobody new. You can decline the request, or they can withdraw it. Nothing was changed.', note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.PROJECT_REQUESTS_NOT_VISIBLE', "A project's requests to join are seen by the people who asked, its owners and administrators. You can read your own requests without naming a project.", note='project-roster, refusal by its code')
w('project-roster.note.owner_set_project', "no owner has set this project's visibility, so it is HIDDEN: a project with no record reads hidden.", note='project-roster, note')
w('refusal.NO_CLASS', 'Your list could not be assembled: something on it does not say what sort of item it is, and showing it without that would put an entry in front of you that nobody can act on. Nothing has been lost and nothing about the record has changed — this is a fault on our side, not something you did.', note='queue, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NO_SUCH_KIND', 'Your list could not be assembled: something on it is described in a word this record does not know, so there is no sentence to show you in place of it. Rather than showing you a line you could not read, the list refuses whole. Nothing has been lost.', note='queue, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.KIND_MISCLASSED', 'Your list could not be assembled: something on it is filed one way and described another, and the difference decides whether setting it aside is a private choice of yours or a change to the record everyone shares. That is not a difference to guess at, so the list refuses until it is right. Nothing has been lost.', note='queue, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.KIND_NOT_PERSONAL', 'Setting this aside would be a change everybody sees rather than a private choice of yours, and that is a decision the team takes together rather than one this control makes. The kinds you can quiet for yourself are listed beside the refusal.', note='queue, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.CLASS_NOT_DISPOSED', 'This is not something the record disposes of. Deferring and dismissing are decisions about something the record NOTICED — its own question — and this item is a different kind of thing: a status item is a fact about our machinery that you quiet for yourself, and a to-do is work a named person owes and leaves every list when it is done. Nothing about it was changed, and it is still in your list. The answer names the act that does reach it.', note='queue, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NO_PROJECT_SCOPE', "Setting this aside is a decision one project takes for its own list, and no project was named for it. Choose the project you are acting for (the item lists the ones it is filed under) and ask again. Nothing was written, and no project's list moved.", note='queue, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.QUEUE_SORT_UNKNOWN', 'Your list cannot be put in that order. It can be sorted by when each item was added, by when it is due, by case or by kind, or left in its usual order, grouped by case. Nothing was read or changed; ask again with one of those.', note='queue, refusal by its code')
w('queue.label.set_aside_project', 'Set it aside for your project', note='queue, label')
w('cdx.unsigned_reason', 'no cryptographic attestation exists over a Wayback capture; this is a dated third-party claim we are trusting, not verifying', note='cdx, unsigned_reason')
w('refusal.NO_SUCH_CASE', 'There is no case by that name that you can see. A case being prepared in a project you are not part of is answered exactly as one that does not exist.', note='case-check, refusal by its code')
w('refusal.NO_ID', 'Say which finding to look for. Nothing was read.', note='case-check, refusal by its code')
